  "_comment": "REAL `bd` output shapes (Constitution Rule 1). CRITICAL (adj-208.1.2.1): each epic's `dependencies` uses the REAL `bd show <epic> --json` shape — a full child issue record with an added `dependency_type` field and its OWN embedded `status` ({id, title, status, issue_type, dependency_type, owner, ...}) — NOT the `bd list` edge tuple {issue_id, depends_on_id, type}. This matters because the production coordination service reads epic progress from `computeEpicProgress`, which sources deps from `bd show`; a list-tuple fixture (the OLD form) tested the assumption, not reality, and stayed green while production read 0 (masked adj-208.1.4). `allBeads` mirrors the `bd list --all` statusMap pass and `openBeads`/`inProgressBeads` mirror `bd list --status` (both bd-list shape, as `getProjectOverview` receives them). Fields carry real CLI keys (owner, created_by, dependency_type) absent from the TS types — fixtures are grounded in the CLI, not the interfaces. See `buildEpicWithChildren` in beads-dependency.ts for the documented show shape.",

